Privacy Policy for Flip-A-Coin

Last Updated: February 8, 2026

This Privacy Policy describes how Flip-A-Coin ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and shares your information when you play our game. We are committed to protecting your privacy and handling your data transparently.

1. Information We Collect

We collect minimal information necessary to provide and improve your gaming experience:

Player Name: When you achieve a personal best streak and choose to enter your name for the Hall of Fame, we collect the full name you provide.
Game Statistics: We record your game progress and achievements, such as your personal best streak, head chance, earnings per heads, combo multiplier, and flip time. These statistics are stored with your Hall of Fame entry.
Local Storage Data: We use your browser's local storage to save your game state (e.g., current money, upgrades, selected skins) and your chosen player name temporarily. This data is stored directly on your device and is not transmitted to our servers unless explicitly submitted for the Hall of Fame.
2. How We Use Your Information

We use the collected information for the following purposes:

To Operate and Improve the Game: This includes managing your game progress, saving your preferences, and enhancing gameplay features.
Hall of Fame: Your player name and personal best streak statistics are used to display your achievements on our public Hall of Fame leaderboard.
Personalization: Your player name is used to display a personalized welcome message on the game's start screen.
Analytics (Aggregated): We may use aggregated and anonymized game statistics to understand how players interact with the game, identify popular features, and make improvements. This data cannot be used to identify you personally.
3. Sharing Your Information

We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties.

Public Display (Hall of Fame): If you choose to submit your name to the Hall of Fame, your provided name, and your personal best streak will be publicly visible on the leaderboard.
Service Providers: We may use third-party services for analytics or platform hosting. These providers are obligated to protect your information and only use it for the purposes we specify.
4. Data Storage and Security

Hall of Fame Data: Information submitted to the Hall of Fame is stored securely on our platform's database. We implement reasonable security measures to protect your data from unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
Local Storage Data: Game state and temporary player name information saved in local storage resides solely on your device. You can clear this data through your browser settings.
5. Your Choices and Rights

Hall of Fame: Submitting your name to the Hall of Fame is optional. If you wish to remove your entry from the Hall of Fame, please contact us using the information below.
Local Storage: You can manage or clear local storage data through your web browser settings.
Access and Correction: If you believe any personal information we hold about you is inaccurate, you may contact us to request corrections.
6. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page. You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes.
